    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by [ a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
            crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "liere (lioure): tape, or narrow strips of cloth, used for binding the edges of a fabric — for veils, sails, bed-hangings etc. (OED s.v. lear2, lyre2; MED s.v. lioure). The name is associated with Lire/Liere in Brabant." ;
